      normMax: 1.5
    Output:
      $t: output
      Resw: 1080
      Resh: 1350
  color: [0.3, 0.5, 0.9]
  tags:
  - tdxn
  tdn_ref: specimen_lab/essence_streams.tdxn
- name: vertical_fibers
  type: baseCOMP
  custom_pars:
    Controls:
    - name: Strands
      style: Int
      default: 56
      min: 4.0
      max: 320.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 4.0
      normMax: 320.0
      help: number of fiber strands in the curtain. Because of the column-fold this costs NOTHING per pixel (no strand loop), so a dense premium bundle is free; raise it freely for a fuller curtain.
    - name: Converge
      style: Float
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      help: how strongly the bundle narrows toward the top. 0 = parallel strands (a flat curtain); higher = strong upward perspective into the haze.
    - name: Bow
      style: Float
      default: 1
      max: 2.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 2.0
      help: amount of gentle per-strand bow so the strands read as relaxed cable, not laser-straight. 0 = dead-straight fibers.
    - name: Glassglow
      style: Float
      default: 1.15
      max: 6.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 6.0
      help: strength of the internal-reflection shimmer gradient along each glass tube. The light-bouncing-in-glass look.
    - name: Pulsespeed
      style: Float
      default: 0.6
      max: 2.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 2.0
      help: how fast the light pulses race UP the strands. 0 freezes them (and drops that time-dependence); higher = near-light-speed streaks.
    - name: Pulsedensity
      style: Int
      default: 4
      min: 1.0
      max: 4.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 1.0
      normMax: 4.0
      help: how many light pulses travel up each strand at once (1-4, the constant loop bound). More = a busier data stream.
    - name: Pulselength
      style: Float
      default: 0.32
      min: 0.02
      max: 0.5
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 0.02
      normMax: 0.5
      help: length of each Gaussian light dash (in vertical UV). Short = crisp countable packets; long = streaking light trails.
    - name: Haze
      style: Float
      default: 2.6
      max: 4.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 4.0
      help: volumetric haze building toward the top of the frame so distant strands dim into fog. Adds vertical depth.
    - name: Linewidth
      style: Float
      default: 0.0045
      min: 0.0012
      max: 0.02
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 0.0012
      normMax: 0.02
      help: base thickness of the glass tube core. Thin = crisp hairline fibers; thicker = heavier glowing tubes. Crisp at any resolution via fwidth().
    - name: Ptprate
      style: Float
      default: 0.5
      min: 0.1
      max: 2.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 0.1
      normMax: 2.0
      help: frequency of the PTP sync pulse all light pulses breathe brighter to in lockstep.
    - name: Bloom
      style: Float
      default: 0.55
      max: 3.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 3.0
      help: intensity of the downsampled bloom glow added back over the pulses. The booth-scale wow knob.
    - name: Bloomwidth
      style: Float
      default: 2.6
      min: 1.0
      max: 4.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 1.0
      normMax: 4.0
      help: the blur step in the 1/4-res bloom pass. Wider = a softer, more atmospheric glow halo (still cheap, since it runs at low res).
    - name: Grain
      style: Float
      default: 1
      max: 2.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 2.0
      help: film-grain amount in the finish pass. Kills banding on the dark gradient at large scale.
    - name: Vignette
      style: Float
      default: 0.95
      max: 1.5
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 1.5
      help: edge darkening so the curtain sits on a premium dark stage.
    Output:
      $t: output
      Resw: 1080
      Resh: 1350
  position: [400, 0]
  color: [0.3, 0.5, 0.9]
  tags:
  - tdxn
  tdn_ref: specimen_lab/vertical_fibers.tdxn
- name: mandelbulb_march
  type: baseCOMP
  custom_pars:
    Mandelbulb:
    - name: Power
      style: Float
      startSection: true
      default: 8
      min: 2.0
      max: 12.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 2.0
      normMax: 12.0
      help: Mandelbulb exponent in z=z^Power+c. 8 is the classic bulb; 2-4 = blobby organic forms; 10-12 = more lobes and finer detail.
    - name: Detail
      style: Float
      label: Surface Detail
      default: 0.6
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      help: Raymarch hit threshold, remapped to a 0.0015->0.0004 epsilon. Higher resolves finer fractal crenellation at more cost near grazing rays.
    - name: Glow
      style: Float
      default: 1
      max: 3.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 3.0
      help: Proximity/iteration glow added along every ray. Close-but-miss rays accumulate an exponential halo. 0 = matte; 3 = ethereal bloom.
    - name: Orbitspeed
      style: Float
      label: Orbit Speed
      startSection: true
      default: 1
      max: 3.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 3.0
      help: Multiplies absTime.seconds into the camera orbit. 0 freezes a still; 1 is a slow cinematic orbit. Only the camera moves -- the fractal math is identical each frame.
    - name: Hue
      style: Float
      default: 0.55
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      help: Base hue offset of the orbit-trap cosine palette. Rotates the whole color identity (surface, glow, rim, background sun) through the spectrum.
    - name: Sunazim
      style: Float
      label: Sun Azimuth
      startSection: true
      default: 35
      min: -180.0
      max: 180.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: -180.0
      normMax: 180.0
      help: Azimuth (degrees) of the key light, converted with elevation into a unit direction so normalize() never sees a zero vector. Rotates where the soft key light and shadow fall.
    - name: Sunelev
      style: Float
      label: Sun Elevation
      default: 45
      min: -10.0
      max: 90.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: -10.0
      normMax: 90.0
      help: Elevation (degrees) of the key light. High = top-down soft light with short shadows; low = dramatic raking light with long soft shadows.
    Output:
      $t: output_2
      Resw: 1080
      Resh: 1350
  position: [800, -800]
  color: [0.3, 0.5, 0.9]
  tags:
  - tdxn
  tdn_ref: specimen_lab/mandelbulb_march.tdxn
- name: prismatic_strata
  type: baseCOMP
  parameters:
    parentshortcut: Specimen
  custom_pars:
    Strata:
    - name: Scale
      style: Float
      label: Noise Scale
      startSection: true
      default: 1.2
      min: 0.3
      max: 4.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 0.3
      normMax: 4.0
      help: Noise features per frame height. Low = a few broad folds; high = many small strata.
    - name: Stretch
      style: Float
      default: 4
      min: 1.0
      max: 6.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 1.0
      normMax: 6.0
      help: Horizontal elongation of the noise. 1 = round blobs; 2.5+ = wide horizontal layers.
    - name: Bands
      style: Float
      default: 2
      min: 0.5
      max: 5.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 0.5
      normMax: 5.0
      help: How many strata (ramp cycles) span the frame height before displacement folds add more.
    - name: Displace
      style: Float
      default: 1.1
      max: 3.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 3.0
      help: How far the noise displaces the ramp, in strata. Past ~1 the layers fold over into extra rims.
    - name: Warp
      style: Float
      default: 0.45
      max: 2.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 2.0
      help: 'Domain warp: a low-frequency noise bends the sample coordinates so the layers curl instead of waving.'
    - name: Detail
      style: Int
      default: 5
      min: 1.0
      max: 6.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 1.0
      normMax: 6.0
      help: fBm octaves. More = finer veins on the layers; costs one noise evaluation each.
    - name: Relief
      style: Float
      default: 0.06
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      help: 'Slope shading from above: compressed layers brighten, overhangs darken. 0 = flat ramp only.'
    - name: Edgesoft
      style: Float
      label: Edge Softness
      default: 0.1
      max: 0.2
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 0.2
      help: Width of the rim edge as a fraction of one stratum. 0 = hard cliff.
    - name: Layers
      style: Float
      label: Fine Layers
      default: 5
      max: 40.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 40.0
      help: 'Fine contour lines per stratum: thin sediment layers that follow every fold of the displaced ramp. 0 = none.'
    - name: Layergain
      style: Float
      label: Layer Gain
      default: 0.14
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      help: Brightness of the fine layers. They read warm in the shadows and pale in the lit zones.
    - name: Grain
      style: Float
      label: Fine Grain
      default: 0.12
      max: 0.5
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 0.5
      help: Fine-scale fibrous noise on the layers (the small end of the scale stack).
    Motion:
    - name: Loopseconds
      style: Float
      label: Loop Seconds
      startSection: true
      default: 1.2
      min: 0.5
      max: 20.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 0.5
      normMax: 20.0
      help: Length of one seamless loop in seconds. The noise travels a closed circle, so the last frame meets the first.
    - name: Scroll
      style: Float
      default: 1
      min: -4.0
      max: 4.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 3.0
      help: Soft pulses that roll DOWN the frame per loop (the ripple). Keep it an integer for a seamless loop. The rims stay put; only the light wave moves.
    - name: Pulses
      style: Float
      label: Pulse Bands
      default: 1.5
      min: 0.25
      max: 4.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 0.25
      normMax: 4.0
      help: How many soft brightness pulses span the frame height. They are the smooth, large-scale wave that rolls down through the layers.
    - name: Pulsegain
      style: Float
      label: Pulse Gain
      default: 0.7
      max: 1.5
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 1.5
      help: Depth of the rolling pulses. 0 = the layers only morph; the rims themselves never move with the pulses.
    - name: Evolution
      style: Float
      default: 0.14
      max: 2.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 2.0
      help: 'Radius of that circle in noise units: how much the layers morph within one loop. 0 = frozen.'
    - name: Seed
      style: Float
      max: 100.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 100.0
      help: Offsets the noise field. Any value gives a different arrangement of layers.
    Look:
    - name: Flow
      style: Float
      startSection: true
      default: 0.06
      max: 0.3
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 0.2
      help: Base displacement of the finished strata by the stratum-scale flow field, as a fraction of the frame height. The whole image swirls with it; Dispersion splits the channels around it.
    - name: Dispersion
      style: Float
      default: 0.12
      max: 1.5
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      help: 'Per-channel share of Flow: red takes 1-d of it, green 1, blue 1+d. 0 = neutral grey warp; 0.45 = orange/azure fringes and stratum-sized warm or cool patches.'
    - name: Tint
      style: Float
      default: 0.9
      max: 1.5
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 1.5
      help: 'Regional warm/cool tint: a stratum-scale field pushes mids and shadows toward rust or steel blue. 0 = neutral.'
    - name: Iridescence
      style: Float
      default: 0.12
      max: 0.5
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 0.5
      help: 'Thin-film hue cycle along the layer coordinate: pastel pink / yellow / cyan bands that follow the folds. 0 = none.'
    - name: Cellscale
      style: Float
      label: Caustic Cells
      default: 18
      min: 4.0
      max: 60.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 4.0
      normMax: 60.0
      help: Caustic web cell count per frame height.
    - name: Cellwidth
      style: Float
      label: Caustic Width
      default: 0.05
      min: 0.01
      max: 0.4
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 0.01
      normMax: 0.4
      help: Thickness of the caustic veins (0..1 of a cell).
    - name: Causticgain
      style: Float
      label: Caustic Gain
      default: 0.5
      max: 2.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 2.0
      help: Brightness added along the caustic veins. 0 = no web.
    - name: Streaklength
      style: Float
      label: Streak Length
      startSection: true
      default: 0.35
      max: 0.6
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 0.6
      help: Half-length of the vertical light streaks, as a fraction of the frame height.
    - name: Streakgain
      style: Float
      label: Streak Gain
      default: 0.9
      max: 3.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 3.0
      help: Brightness of the streaks. 0 = none.
    - name: Streakthreshold
      style: Float
      label: Streak Threshold
      default: 0.12
      max: 0.5
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 0.5
      help: Only thin features brighter than their surroundings by this much seed a streak.
    - name: Glow
      style: Float
      startSection: true
      default: 0.22
      max: 1.5
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 1.5
      help: A broad drifting light field that lifts regions toward white (the backlit fog).
    - name: Bloom
      style: Float
      default: 0.25
      max: 3.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMax: 3.0
      help: Bloom TOP intensity on the final image.
    Output:
    - name: Resw
      style: Int
      label: Width
      startSection: true
      default: 1920
      min: 256.0
      max: 7680.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 256.0
      normMax: 7680.0
      help: Render width (px). Drives every resolution-bearing op in this specimen.
    - name: Resh
      style: Int
      label: Height
      default: 1080
      min: 256.0
      max: 7680.0
      clampMin: true
      clampMax: true
      normMin: 256.0
      normMax: 7680.0
      help: Render height (px).
  position: [1600, 0]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  children:
  - name: out1
    type: outTOP
    parameters:
      label: =me.name
    flags:
    - display
    position: [5400, 0]
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
    inputs:
    - bloom
  - name: bloom
    type: bloomTOP
    parameters:
      preblacklevel: 0.8
      minbloomradius: 0.15
      maxbloomradius: 0.8
      bloomthreshold: 0
      bloomintensity: =parent.Specimen.par.Bloom.eval()
    position: [5000, 0]
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
    inputs:
    - glsl_streaks
  - name: glsl_prism
    type: glslTOP
    parameters:
      pixeldat: glsl_prism_pixel
      computedat: glsl_prism_compute
      inputextenduv: mirror
      premultrgbbyalpha: false
    sequences:
      vec:
      - name: uPrism
        valuex: =parent.Specimen.par.Flow.eval()
        valuey: =parent.Specimen.par.Dispersion.eval()
        valuez: =parent.Specimen.par.Streakthreshold.eval()
      - name: uDetail
        valuex: =parent.Specimen.par.Causticgain.eval()
        valuey: =parent.Specimen.par.Layergain.eval()
        valuez: 0
        valuew: 0
    position: [2800, 0]
    inputs:
    - glsl_strata
    - renderselect_disp
  - name: glsl_strata
    type: glslTOP
    parameters:
      pixeldat: glsl_strata_pixel
      computedat: glsl_strata_compute
      inputextenduv: hold
      numcolorbufs: 3
      outputresolution: custom
      resolutionw: =parent.Specimen.par.Resw.eval()
      resolutionh: =parent.Specimen.par.Resh.eval()
    sequences:
      vec:
      - name: uField
        valuex: =parent.Specimen.par.Scale.eval()
        valuey: =parent.Specimen.par.Stretch.eval()
        valuez: =parent.Specimen.par.Warp.eval()
        valuew: =parent.Specimen.par.Detail.eval()
      - name: uStrata
        valuex: =parent.Specimen.par.Bands.eval()
        valuey: =parent.Specimen.par.Displace.eval()
        valuez: =parent.Specimen.par.Relief.eval()
        valuew: =parent.Specimen.par.Edgesoft.eval()
      - name: uTime
        valuex: =(absTime.seconds % parent.Specimen.par.Loopseconds.eval()) / parent.Specimen.par.Loopseconds.eval()
        valuey: =parent.Specimen.par.Evolution.eval()
        valuez: =parent.Specimen.par.Seed.eval()
        valuew: =parent.Specimen.par.Glow.eval()
      - name: uCaustic
        valuex: =parent.Specimen.par.Cellscale.eval()
        valuey: =parent.Specimen.par.Cellwidth.eval()
        valuez: =parent.Specimen.par.Tint.eval()
        valuew: =parent.Specimen.par.Iridescence.eval()
      - name: uLayers
        valuex: =parent.Specimen.par.Layers.eval()
        valuey: =parent.Specimen.par.Scroll.eval()
        valuez: =parent.Specimen.par.Grain.eval()
        valuew: 0
      - name: uPulse
        valuex: =parent.Specimen.par.Pulses.eval()
        valuey: =parent.Specimen.par.Pulsegain.eval()
        valuez: 0
        valuew: 0
    flags:
    - viewer
    position: [1400, 0]
    inputs:
    - ramp_strata
  - name: ramp_strata
    type: rampTOP
    parameters:
      dat: ramp_strata_keys
      color1: 0.400000006
      color2: 0.2700000107
      color3: 0.200000003
      extendleft: hold
      outputresolution: custom
      resolutionw: 512
      resolutionh: 4
      format: rgba16float
    position: [400, 0]
    size: [130, 90]
    color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  - name: glsl_streaks
    type: glslTOP
    parameters:
      pixeldat: glsl_streaks_pixel
      computedat: glsl_streaks_compute
      inputextenduv: mirror
    sequences:
      vec:
      - name: uStreak
        valuex: =parent.Specimen.par.Streaklength.eval()
        valuey: =parent.Specimen.par.Streakgain.eval()
    position: [4000, 0]
    inputs:
    - glsl_prism
    - renderselect_grad
  - name: glsl_prism_info
    type: infoDAT
    parameters:
      op: glsl_prism
    position: [2950, -120]
    dock: glsl_prism
    dat_read_only: true
  - name: glsl_prism_pixel
    type: textDAT
    parameters:
      extension: frag
    flags:
    - viewer
    position: [2800, -120]
    dock: glsl_prism
    dat_content: |
      // glsl_prism -- the rainbow. A Displace TOP run three times: a smooth base displacement field
      // (Flow) warps the whole soft image, and each channel takes a different share of it (Dispersion):
      // red 1-d, green 1, blue 1+d. Where the field is strong, red and blue land tens of pixels apart,
      // so every gradient picks up a regional warm or cool tint and every edge comes apart into
      // orange / azure fringes; where the field is weak the channels line up and the image stays neutral.
      // The detail (caustic web, fine layers) is composited AFTER the split, sampled at the green
      // position so it stays glued to the layers -- crisp lines that were split would leave green and
      // magenta copies the reference never shows.
      // Input 0 = soft strata (glsl_strata buffer 0). Input 1 = field (buffer 1 via renderselect_disp):
      // xy = flow vector encoded 0.5 + 0.5 * w, z = web mask, w = fine layers.
      // Alpha out = streak seeds for glsl_streaks: thin bright vertical features (a horizontal high-pass
      // of the base and of the web, weighted toward bright pixels, dilated a few px along y so the streak
      // pass cannot step over one, gated per column so the streaks cluster).
      uniform vec4 uPrism;    // x = Flow (base displacement, fraction of frame height)  y = Dispersion (per-channel share)  z = Streakthreshold  w unused
      uniform vec4 uDetail;   // x = Causticgain  y = Layergain  z,w unused
      out vec4 fragColor;

      float lum(vec3 c){ return dot(c, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722)); }
      float lumAt(vec2 uv){ return lum(texture(sTD2DInputs[0], uv).rgb); }
      float webAt(vec2 uv){ return texture(sTD2DInputs[1], uv).z; }

      float seedAt(vec2 uv, vec2 px){
          vec2 dx = vec2(3.0 * px.x, 0.0);
          float c = lumAt(uv);
          float hpBase = c - 0.5 * (lumAt(uv - dx) + lumAt(uv + dx));
          float hpWeb  = webAt(uv) - 0.5 * (webAt(uv - dx) + webAt(uv + dx));
          float hp = max(hpBase, 0.5 * hpWeb);
          return smoothstep(uPrism.z, uPrism.z + 0.12, hp) * smoothstep(0.45, 0.9, c);
      }

      void main(){
          vec2 uv  = vUV.st;
          vec2 res = uTD2DInfos[0].res.zw;                          // width, height
          vec2 px  = uTD2DInfos[0].res.xy;                          // 1/width, 1/height
          vec2 w   = texture(sTD2DInputs[1], uv).xy * 2.0 - 1.0;    // decode -1..1
          vec2 d   = uPrism.x * w * vec2(res.y / res.x, 1.0);       // height-relative -> uv (x shrinks by aspect)
          float share = uPrism.y;
          float r = texture(sTD2DInputs[0], uv + d * (1.0 - share)).r;
          float g = texture(sTD2DInputs[0], uv + d).g;
          float b = texture(sTD2DInputs[0], uv + d * (1.0 + share)).b;
          vec3 col = vec3(r, g, b);
          float L = lum(col);

          // detail rides with the green channel
          vec4 f = texture(sTD2DInputs[1], uv + d);
          float fine = f.w;
          col *= 1.0 + uDetail.y * (fine - 0.3) * mix(vec3(1.1, 0.95, 0.85), vec3(1.0), smoothstep(0.1, 0.6, L));
          float web = f.z;
          col += web * uDetail.x * mix(0.8, 0.02, smoothstep(0.15, 0.8, L)) * vec3(1.0, 0.75, 0.55) * (0.5 + col);

          float seed = 0.0;
          for(int j = -2; j <= 2; j++){
              seed = max(seed, seedAt(uv + d + vec2(0.0, float(j) * 2.0 * px.y), px));
          }
          float colBin = floor(uv.x * res.x / 3.0);
          float gate = fract(sin(colBin * 12.9898) * 43758.5453);
          seed *= smoothstep(0.62, 0.85, gate);

          fragColor = TDOutputSwizzle(vec4(col, seed));
      }
    dat_content_format: text
  - name: glsl_strata_info
    type: infoDAT
    parameters:
      op: glsl_strata
    position: [1550, -120]
    dock: glsl_strata
    dat_read_only: true
  - name: ramp_strata_keys
    type: tableDAT
